face — face must occupy 70–80% of the frame, both ears visible, neutral expression, no smile that bares teeth.\n• Signature in pencil or blue gel pen on lined paper — use a black ballpoint on plain white paper, then scan or photograph.\n• Photo must NOT be older than 3 months and must show the capture date printed at the bottom\n\nSpecification table (quick reference):\n\nField         | Requirement\n------------- | --------------------------------\nPhoto size    | 3.5 × 4.5 cm — 100 × 120 pixels\nPhoto weight  | 20 KB to 50 KB\nPhoto format  | JPEG\nBackground    | white or light\nSignature size| 4.0 × 2.0 cm — 140 × 60 pixels\nSignature wt  | 10 KB to 20 KB\nSignature fmt | JPEG\nIssuing body  | Staff Selection Commission (SSC)\nPortal        | ssc.gov.in"}, {"heading": "Privacy, security and why VexaTool is safe for government forms", "body_md": "Your SSC CGL (Combined Graduate Level) photograph is sensitive personal data. VexaTool processes the image entirely in your browser using the HTML5 Canvas API — the file never leaves your device, is never uploaded to any server, and is not stored, logged or shared. Closing the tab erases everything. There are no accounts, no email capture, and no watermarks on the output. This makes the tool safe to use on shared computers in a cyber cafe and compliant with the Staff Selection Commission (SSC)''s expectation that the candidate himself or herself prepares the file."}, {"heading": "Acceptable formats, EXIF and colour profiles", "body_md": "Most Indian government portals accept JPEG only. PNG is rejected at IBPS, SBI, SSC and UPSC, even though the file is smaller, because their image validator expects baseline JPEG markers. VexaTool always writes a baseline JPEG with the sRGB colour profile and no EXIF metadata — this is the safest combination across every portal we have tested.\n\nIf your source is HEIC (iPhone) or AVIF (modern Android), the tool decodes it transparently. If your source is a PDF page, use the PDF-to-JPG converter first, then bring the JPG here. If your source is a screenshot, retake the photo — screenshots include device UI chrome and are almost always rejected by face-detection validators.\n\nFinally, a note on Adobe RGB and CMYK: studio cameras sometimes embed these wider colour profiles. They look identical on screen but trigger rejections on older portals. VexaTool strips them on export, so the output is universally accepted."}]'::jsonb, faqs = '[{"q": "Will the resized photo be accepted by the SSC CGL (Combined Graduate Level) portal?", "a": "Yes — provided you keep the dimension at 3.5 × 4.5 cm — 100 × 120 pixels, the format as JPEG, the file size inside 20 KB to 50 KB, and a white or light background. The portal validates these four properties; nothing else is checked at upload."}, {"q": "Why does my SSC CGL (Combined Graduate Level) application say ''invalid photograph'' even after resizing?", "a": "The most common cause is an extra colour-profile (CMYK / sRGB tag) added by mobile camera apps. VexaTool strips this on export. If the error persists, re-take the photo against a white or light wall — the Staff Selection Commission (SSC) face-detection rejects busy backgrounds even when the file size is correct."}, {"q": "Is there a separate tool for the signature?", "a": "You can use the same resizer with the signature target preset: 4.0 × 2.0 cm — 140 × 60 pixels, 10 KB to 20 KB, JPEG. Sign in black ink on plain white paper, photograph in good light, then crop tight around the signature before resizing."}, {"q": "How recent should the photograph be?", "a": "The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) requires a photograph taken within the last three months. Photo must NOT be older than 3 months and must show the capture date printed at the bottom."}, {"q": "Is the tool free and does it require sign-up?", "a": "VexaTool is completely free, has no account requirement, no daily limit and no watermark. You can process as many photos as you need."}, {"q": "Does the tool work on a mobile phone for the SSC CGL (Combined Graduate Level) form?", "a": "Yes — the resizer is fully responsive and runs in Chrome, Safari, Firefox and the in-app browsers of Gmail and WhatsApp. Most candidates resize the photo on the same phone they will use to submit the form."}]'::jsonb, internal_links = '[{"href": "/govt-job-photo-resize", "label": "Govt Job Photo Resizer (general)"}, {"href": "/passport-photo-resize", "label": "Passport-Size Photo Maker"}, {"href": "/aadhaar-photo-resize", "label": "Aadhaar Photo Resizer (50 KB)"}, {"href": "/image-resizer", "label": "Image Resizer (custom dimensions)"}, {"href": "/compress-image", "label": "Compress Image (any KB target)"}, {"href": "/jpg-to-pdf", "label": "Convert JPG to PDF (form attachments)"}, {"href": "/background-remover", "label": "Background Remover (white background)"}, {"href": "/image-format-converter", "label": "HEIC / PNG → JPG converter"}]'::jsonb, breadcrumbs = '[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "Image Tools", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "Govt Photo Resizers", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "SSC CGL (Combined Graduate Level) Photo Resizer", "href": "#"}]'::jsonb, parent_tool_slug = 'govt-job-photo-resize', canonical_url = 'https://vexatool.com/ssc-cgl-photo-resizer', updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'ssc-cgl-photo-resizer';

