ors.\n\nFinally, a note on Adobe RGB and CMYK: studio cameras sometimes embed these wider colour profiles. They look identical on screen but trigger rejections on older portals. VexaTool strips them on export, so the output is universally accepted."}]'::jsonb, faqs = '[{"q": "Will the resized photo be accepted by the SSC CHSL (10+2) portal?", "a": "Yes — provided you keep the dimension at 3.5 × 4.5 cm — 100 × 120 pixels, the format as JPEG, the file size inside 20 KB to 50 KB, and a white or light background. The portal validates these four properties; nothing else is checked at upload."}, {"q": "Why does my SSC CHSL (10+2) application say ''invalid photograph'' even after resizing?", "a": "The most common cause is an extra colour-profile (CMYK / sRGB tag) added by mobile camera apps. VexaTool strips this on export. If the error persists, re-take the photo against a white or light wall — the Staff Selection Commission (SSC) face-detection rejects busy backgrounds even when the file size is correct."}, {"q": "Is there a separate tool for the signature?", "a": "You can use the same resizer with the signature target preset: 4.0 × 2.0 cm — 140 × 60 pixels, 10 KB to 20 KB, JPEG. Sign in black ink on plain white paper, photograph in good light, then crop tight around the signature before resizing."}, {"q": "How recent should the photograph be?", "a": "The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) requires a photograph taken within the last three months. Black-and-white photos are rejected."}, {"q": "Is the tool free and does it require sign-up?", "a": "VexaTool is completely free, has no account requirement, no daily limit and no watermark. You can process as many photos as you need."}, {"q": "Does the tool work on a mobile phone for the SSC CHSL (10+2) form?", "a": "Yes — the resizer is fully responsive and runs in Chrome, Safari, Firefox and the in-app browsers of Gmail and WhatsApp. Most candidates resize the photo on the same phone they will use to submit the form."}]'::jsonb, internal_links = '[{"href": "/govt-job-photo-resize", "label": "Govt Job Photo Resizer (general)"}, {"href": "/passport-photo-resize", "label": "Passport-Size Photo Maker"}, {"href": "/aadhaar-photo-resize", "label": "Aadhaar Photo Resizer (50 KB)"}, {"href": "/image-resizer", "label": "Image Resizer (custom dimensions)"}, {"href": "/compress-image", "label": "Compress Image (any KB target)"}, {"href": "/jpg-to-pdf", "label": "Convert JPG to PDF (form attachments)"}, {"href": "/background-remover", "label": "Background Remover (white background)"}, {"href": "/image-format-converter", "label": "HEIC / PNG → JPG converter"}]'::jsonb, breadcrumbs = '[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "Image Tools", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "Govt Photo Resizers", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "SSC CHSL (10+2) Photo Resizer", "href": "#"}]'::jsonb, parent_tool_slug = 'govt-job-photo-resize', canonical_url = 'https://vexatool.com/ssc-chsl-photo-resizer', updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'ssc-chsl-photo-resizer';

UPDATE programmatic_seo_pages SET seo_title = 'SBI PO / Clerk / SO Photo Resize Online (200 × 230 pixels, 20 KB to 50 KB) | VexaTool', meta_description = 'Resize your SBI PO / Clerk / SO photograph and signature to the official State Bank of India (SBI) specification — 200 × 230 pixels, 20 KB to 50 KB, JPEG. 100% in-browser, instant, free.', h1 = 'SBI PO / Clerk / SO Photo & Signature Resizer — Online, Free, No Login', intro_md = 'The SBI PO / Clerk / SO application form on sbi.co.in/careers rejects almost half of all uploads on the first attempt — and the reason is almost always the photograph. The State Bank of India (SBI) expects the image at exactly 200 × 230 pixels in JPEG format with a file size between 20 KB to 50 KB, and the signature at 140 × 60 pixels between 10 KB to 20 KB. Most camera apps and scanners produce files that are five to ten times larger than that. This page is a step-by-step resizer built around the exact SBI PO / Clerk / SO specification: upload, crop to the correct aspect ratio, compress to the right file size, and download — all inside your browser, with no upload to any server, no watermark, and no login.', sections = '[{"heading": "Official SBI PO / Clerk / SO photograph & signature specification", "body_md": "Before resizing anything, lock down the rules the State Bank of India (SBI) actually publishes:\n\n• Photograph dimension — 200 × 230 pixels.\n• Photograph file size — 20 KB to 50 KB.\n• Photograph format — JPEG.\n• Background — light, preferably white.\n• Signature dimension — 140 × 60 pixels.\n• Signature file size — 10 KB to 20 KB.\n• Signature format — JPEG.\n• Additional rule — Left thumb impression (240 × 240 px, 20–50 KB) + hand-written declaration (800 × 400 px, 50–100 KB) required.\n\nThese numbers come straight from the latest SBI Career online application notification on sbi.co.in/careers. Always cross-check the active notification PDF before you upload, because the State Bank of India (SBI) occasionally tightens the file-size band (the most common change is dropping the upper limit). If your photo is even 1 KB above the maximum or 5 pixels off, the portal will throw a generic “invalid file” error without telling you which rule failed."}, {"heading": "How to resize your SBI PO / Clerk / SO photo step by step", "body_md": "1. Take a fresh photograph in front of a light, preferably white wall, in even daylight, with your face filling about 70–80% of the frame. A phone in portrait mode works as well as a studio camera as long as the background stays clean.\n2. Open the VexaTool Aadhaar / passport / govt-job photo resizer linked below and drop your image in.\n3. Set the target dimension to 200 × 230 pixels and the output format to JPEG.\n4. Drag the crop box so the eyes sit on the upper third of the frame and both ears are inside.\n5. Set the maximum file size to the upper limit (50 KB). VexaTool runs an iterative JPEG quality search to land just under that cap without going below the minimum.\n6. Download the file. Repeat steps 2–6 for your signature using 140 × 60 pixels and 10 KB to 20 KB.\n7. Upload both files in the SBI Career online application portal and refresh the preview — the State Bank of India (SBI) portal usually shows a small thumbnail; if it shows correctly, the file passed validation."}, {"heading": "Common rejection reasons on the SBI PO / Clerk / SO portal", "body_md": "• File too large — most candidates upload a phone JPEG of 1–3 MB. Compressing to 20 KB to 50 KB fixes this.\n• Wrong aspect ratio — the SBI PO / Clerk / SO crop must be exactly 200 × 230 pixels. A square crop or a 4:3 selfie is rejected silently.\n• Coloured background — only light, preferably white is accepted. Office walls with posters or curtains are rejected.\n• Group / cropped face — face must occupy 70–80% of the frame, both ears visible, neutral expression, no smile that bares teeth.\n• Signature in pencil or blue gel pen on lined paper — use a black ballpoint on plain white paper, then scan or photograph.\n• Left thumb impression (240 × 240 px, 20–50 KB) + hand-written declaration (800 × 400 px, 50–100 KB) required\n\nSpecification table (quick reference):\n\nField         | Requirement\n------------- | --------------------------------\nPhoto size    | 200 × 230 pixels\nPhoto weight  | 20 KB to 50 KB\nPhoto format  | JPEG\nBackground    | light, preferably white\nSignature size| 140 × 60 pixels\nSignature wt  | 10 KB to 20 KB\nSignature fmt | JPEG\nIssuing body  | State Bank of India (SBI)\nPortal        | sbi.co.in/careers"}, {"heading": "Privacy, security and why VexaTool is safe for government forms", "body_md": "Your SBI PO / Clerk / SO photograph is sensitive personal data. VexaTool processes the image entirely in your browser using the HTML5 Canvas API — the file never leaves your device, is never uploaded to any server, and is not stored, logged or shared. Closing the tab erases everything. There are no accounts, no email capture, and no watermarks on the output. This makes the tool safe to use on shared computers in a cyber cafe and compliant with the State Bank of India (SBI)''s expectation that the candidate himself or herself prepares the file."}, {"heading": "Acceptable formats, EXIF and colour profiles", "body_md": "Most Indian government portals accept JPEG only. PNG is rejected at IBPS, SBI, SSC and UPSC, even though the file is smaller, because their image validator expects baseline JPEG markers. VexaTool always writes a baseline JPEG with the sRGB colour profile and no EXIF metadata — this is the safest combination across every portal we have tested.\n\nIf your source is HEIC (iPhone) or AVIF (modern Android), the tool decodes it transparently. If your source is a PDF page, use the PDF-to-JPG converter first, then bring the JPG here. If your source is a screenshot, retake the photo — screenshots include device UI chrome and are almost always rejected by face-detection validators.\n\nFinally, a note on Adobe RGB and CMYK: studio cameras sometimes embed these wider colour profiles. They look identical on screen but trigger rejections on older portals. VexaTool strips them on export, so the output is universally accepted."}]'::jsonb, faqs = '[{"q": "Will the resized photo be accepted by the SBI PO / Clerk / SO portal?", "a": "Yes — provided you keep the dimension at 200 × 230 pixels, the format as JPEG, the file size inside 20 KB to 50 KB, and a light, preferably white background. The portal validates these four properties; nothing else is checked at upload."}, {"q": "Why does my SBI PO / Clerk / SO application say ''invalid photograph'' even after resizing?", "a": "The most common cause is an extra colour-profile (CMYK / sRGB tag) added by mobile camera apps. VexaTool strips this on export. If the error persists, re-take the photo against a light, preferably white wall — the State Bank of India (SBI) face-detection rejects busy backgrounds even when the file size is correct."}, {"q": "Is there a separate tool for the signature?", "a": "You can use the same resizer with the signature target preset: 140 × 60 pixels, 10 KB to 20 KB, JPEG. Sign in black ink on plain white paper, photograph in good light, then crop tight around the signature before resizing."}, {"q": "How recent should the photograph be?", "a": "The State Bank of India (SBI) requires a photograph taken within the last three months. Left thumb impression (240 × 240 px, 20–50 KB) + hand-written declaration (800 × 400 px, 50–100 KB) required."}, {"q": "Is the tool free and does it require sign-up?", "a": "VexaTool is completely free, has no account requirement, no daily limit and no watermark. You can process as many photos as you need."}, {"q": "Does the tool work on a mobile phone for the SBI PO / Clerk / SO form?", "a": "Yes — the resizer is fully responsive and runs in Chrome, Safari, Firefox and the in-app browsers of Gmail and WhatsApp. Most candidates resize the photo on the same phone they will use to submit the form."}]'::jsonb, internal_links = '[{"href": "/govt-job-photo-resize", "label": "Govt Job Photo Resizer (general)"}, {"href": "/passport-photo-resize", "label": "Passport-Size Photo Maker"}, {"href": "/aadhaar-photo-resize", "label": "Aadhaar Photo Resizer (50 KB)"}, {"href": "/image-resizer", "label": "Image Resizer (custom dimensions)"}, {"href": "/compress-image", "label": "Compress Image (any KB target)"}, {"href": "/jpg-to-pdf", "label": "Convert JPG to PDF (form attachments)"}, {"href": "/background-remover", "label": "Background Remover (white background)"}, {"href": "/image-format-converter", "label": "HEIC / PNG → JPG converter"}]'::jsonb, breadcrumbs = '[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "Image Tools", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "Govt Photo Resizers", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "SBI PO / Clerk / SO Photo Resizer", "href": "#"}]'::jsonb, parent_tool_slug = 'govt-job-photo-resize', canonical_url = 'https://vexatool.com/sbi-po-photo-resizer', updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'sbi-po-photo-resizer';

