DF stream compression is non-linear — the final size depends on font dictionaries and image entropy. VexaTool runs a second pass automatically if the first overshoots 150 KB."}, {"q": "Can I batch-compress multiple PDFs?", "a": "Yes. Drag and drop several files at once; each one is compressed sequentially using the same target preset and downloaded as a zip."}, {"q": "Is the tool free and private?", "a": "Completely free, no sign-up, no watermark. Processing happens in your browser; nothing is uploaded."}]'::jsonb, internal_links = '[{"href": "/compress-pdf", "label": "PDF Compressor (custom size)"}, {"href": "/merge-pdf", "label": "Merge PDF Files"}, {"href": "/split-pdf", "label": "Split PDF Pages"}, {"href": "/jpg-to-pdf", "label": "JPG to PDF"}, {"href": "/pdf-to-jpg", "label": "PDF to JPG"}, {"href": "/word-to-pdf", "label": "Word to PDF"}, {"href": "/file-compressor", "label": "Universal File Compressor"}, {"href": "/pdf-tools", "label": "All PDF Tools"}]'::jsonb, breadcrumbs = '[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "PDF Tools", "href": "/pdf-tools"}, {"name": "Compress PDF", "href": "/compress-pdf"}, {"name": "Compress PDF to 150", "href": "#"}]'::jsonb, parent_tool_slug = 'compress-pdf', canonical_url = 'https://vexatool.com/compress-pdf-to-150kb', updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'compress-pdf-to-150kb';

UPDATE programmatic_seo_pages SET seo_title = 'Compress PDF to 200 KB Online Free — Exact File Size | VexaTool', meta_description = 'Reduce any PDF to under 200 KB without losing readability. Designed for passport Seva annexures, GST registration documents, and SBI online KYC where the per-document limit is 200 KB. 100% in-browser, no upload, no watermark, no login.', h1 = 'Compress PDF to 200 KB Online — Free, In-Browser, No Email', intro_md = 'A surprising number of Indian and global form portals still impose a hard 200 KB cap on PDF uploads. If your PDF is even 1 KB above the limit the upload silently fails — the portal usually just says ''file too large'' without telling you the exact ceiling. This page is a focused compressor that targets the 200 KB threshold specifically, using a multi-pass strategy (image down-sampling, JPEG quality search, stream re-encoding and metadata stripping) to land just under 200 KB while keeping the document fully readable. It runs entirely in your browser, never uploads the file, and works for passport Seva annexures, GST registration documents, and SBI online KYC where the per-document limit is 200 KB.', sections = '[{"heading": "What does ''200 KB PDF'' actually mean?", "body_md": "Most exam and KYC portals reject anything above 200 KB, but rejecting at exactly 200 KB is uncommon — the safe target is roughly 90–95% of the cap, i.e. between 170 KB and 190 KB. Going far below the cap also helps if the portal recompresses the file after upload (some PSC portals do). On VexaTool the compressor defaults to that safe band: it will not deliver an unreadable 60 KB output just to be ''small''.\n\nCompression level for this page: moderate. The lower the target size, the more aggressive the image down-sampling. For pure-text PDFs (forms, bonafide letters, agreements) you can hit any of the buckets without quality loss. For scanned PDFs the ceiling depends on the number of pages — a 10-page scanned PDF at 200 KB will look noticeably softer than a 2-page one."}, {"heading": "How to compress a PDF to 200 KB step by step", "body_md": "1. Open the VexaTool PDF compressor (link below) and drop your file. There is no size limit on the input.\n2. The tool inspects the PDF and reports the current size, page count and whether the pages are vector text or scanned images.\n3. Pick the ''200 KB'' preset from the target dropdown. VexaTool runs an iterative search:\n   – Pass 1 strips unused fonts, embedded thumbnails, JavaScript and metadata.\n   – Pass 2 down-samples images to 200 DPI maximum.\n   – Pass 3 re-encodes images as progressive JPEG with a quality value chosen by binary search to land in the target band.\n   – Pass 4 re-runs the search if the result is still above 200 KB.\n4. Preview every page in the side panel and confirm legibility, then download.\n5. If the output is unreadable, raise the target one bucket (for example move from 200 KB to the next bucket up) — quality matters more than shaving off a few KB."}, {"heading": "Where the 200 KB limit actually appears in real life", "body_md": "The 200 KB ceiling is most common in: passport Seva annexures, GST registration documents, and SBI online KYC where the per-document limit is 200 KB.\n\nComparison of common PDF size caps:\n\nCap     | Typical use case\n------- | --------------------------\n50 KB   | SSC, single-page mark sheets\n150 KB  | UPSC supporting documents\n200 KB  | Passport Seva, GST docs\n300 KB  | EPF, ITR enclosures\n500 KB  | CAT / GATE counselling\n1 MB    | Visa, MNC job portals\n\nIf you do not know the exact cap your portal enforces, target the next-lower bucket — uploads always succeed under the cap, never over it."}, {"heading": "Privacy, quality and what makes VexaTool different", "body_md": "VexaTool runs the entire compression pipeline through pdfjs-dist and pdf-lib in your browser. The PDF never crosses the network, is never queued on a server, and is purged from memory the moment you close the tab. There is no account, no email capture, no watermark, and no daily quota. This makes the tool safe for sensitive documents like Aadhaar, PAN, bank statements, ITR acknowledgements and salary slips that you would not want to upload to a third-party server."}, {"heading": "Troubleshooting and verifying the result", "body_md": "After downloading, verify three things before you upload:\n\n1. File size — right-click in your file manager and confirm it is at or below the target. Some Windows preview panels round to the nearest 10 KB; trust the Properties dialog instead.\n2. Page integrity — open in any PDF reader and scroll every page. Tables, signatures and stamps should remain crisp.\n3. Text searchability — for OCR-scanned PDFs, hit Ctrl+F and search for a word you can see. If search fails, the OCR layer was dropped by aggressive compression; re-run with a larger target bucket.\n\nIf the upload still fails on the portal, the cause is almost always one of: (a) the portal also enforces a page-count cap (e.g. 2 pages max); (b) the portal expects A4 page size and rejects Letter; (c) the file name contains spaces or non-ASCII characters. Rename to a simple name like document.pdf, set page size to A4 if needed, and retry."}]'::jsonb, faqs = '[{"q": "Will the 200 KB output still be readable?", "a": "Yes for text-heavy PDFs. For scanned PDFs of more than 5 pages at the 200 KB target the text may look slightly soft but remains legible at 100% zoom. If you need archival quality, pick the next-larger bucket."}, {"q": "Is there a page limit?", "a": "No. The compressor handles single-page certificates as well as 200-page report PDFs. Large documents simply take a few more seconds to finish in-browser."}, {"q": "Does compression remove signatures or form fields?", "a": "No. Digital signatures, AcroForm fields, hyperlinks and bookmarks are preserved. Only embedded thumbnails, unused fonts and metadata are stripped."}, {"q": "Why does the output sometimes overshoot the target by a few KB?", "a": "PDF stream compression is non-linear — the final size depends on font dictionaries and image entropy. VexaTool runs a second pass automatically if the first overshoots 200 KB."}, {"q": "Can I batch-compress multiple PDFs?", "a": "Yes. Drag and drop several files at once; each one is compressed sequentially using the same target preset and downloaded as a zip."}, {"q": "Is the tool free and private?", "a": "Completely free, no sign-up, no watermark. Processing happens in your browser; nothing is uploaded."}]'::jsonb, internal_links = '[{"href": "/compress-pdf", "label": "PDF Compressor (custom size)"}, {"href": "/merge-pdf", "label": "Merge PDF Files"}, {"href": "/split-pdf", "label": "Split PDF Pages"}, {"href": "/jpg-to-pdf", "label": "JPG to PDF"}, {"href": "/pdf-to-jpg", "label": "PDF to JPG"}, {"href": "/word-to-pdf", "label": "Word to PDF"}, {"href": "/file-compressor", "label": "Universal File Compressor"}, {"href": "/pdf-tools", "label": "All PDF Tools"}]'::jsonb, breadcrumbs = '[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "PDF Tools", "href": "/pdf-tools"}, {"name": "Compress PDF", "href": "/compress-pdf"}, {"name": "Compress PDF to 200", "href": "#"}]'::jsonb, parent_tool_slug = 'compress-pdf', canonical_url = 'https://vexatool.com/compress-pdf-to-200kb', updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'compress-pdf-to-200kb';

