count requirement. Output files are watermark-free."}]'::jsonb, internal_links = '[{"href": "/compress-image", "label": "Image Compressor (any KB)"}, {"href": "/image-resizer", "label": "Image Resizer (custom dimensions)"}, {"href": "/image-format-converter", "label": "Image Format Converter"}, {"href": "/background-remover", "label": "Background Remover"}, {"href": "/passport-photo-resize", "label": "Passport-Size Photo Maker"}, {"href": "/aadhaar-photo-resize", "label": "Aadhaar Photo Resizer"}, {"href": "/govt-job-photo-resize", "label": "Govt Job Photo Resizer"}, {"href": "/image-tools", "label": "All Image Tools"}]'::jsonb, breadcrumbs = '[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "Image Tools", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "Compress Image", "href": "/compress-image"}, {"name": "Compress to 100 KB", "href": "#"}]'::jsonb, parent_tool_slug = 'compress-image', canonical_url = 'https://vexatool.com/compress-jpeg-to-100kb', updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'compress-jpeg-to-100kb';

UPDATE programmatic_seo_pages SET seo_title = 'Resize Image to 20 KB Online Free — Exact File Size | VexaTool', meta_description = 'Resize and compress any photo to under 20 KB. Designed for exam photo slots that combine a pixel-cap (e.g. 200×230) with a 20 KB file-size cap — most SSC and railway portals. 100% in-browser, no upload, no watermark, no login.', h1 = 'Resize Image to 20 KB Online — Smart Pixel + Quality Resize', intro_md = 'Form portals across India still cap photo uploads at very specific sizes. 20 KB is one of the most common — it is the upper limit for exam photo slots that combine a pixel-cap (e.g. 200×230) with a 20 KB file-size cap — most SSC and railway portals. This page is a focused resizer that targets exactly 20 KB, runs entirely in your browser, and is free of accounts, watermarks or upload queues.', sections = '[{"heading": "Why portals enforce a 20 KB image limit", "body_md": "Government and exam portals throttle photo uploads to keep their storage and bandwidth bills predictable. At national scale, 1 crore applicants uploading 5 MB photos would cost the agency 50 TB of storage per cycle — capping at 20 KB reduces that to a few hundred GB. The cap is enforced server-side; client-side validation is rarely friendly, so the only way to know your file passed is to upload, get the green tick, and refresh.\n\nResizing lowers both the pixel dimensions and the file weight. That is the right strategy when the portal enforces a pixel-cap (e.g. 200×230) together with a 20 KB file-size cap — simply compressing the original 4000×3000 photo to 20 KB would make it unreadable. VexaTool first scales the longer edge down, then runs the JPEG-quality search."}, {"heading": "How to resize an image to 20 KB step by step", "body_md": "1. Open the VexaTool image resizer linked below and drop your photo. Input can be HEIC, JPG, PNG, WebP, or BMP.\n2. Set the target pixel dimensions to match the portal spec (e.g. 200×230 for IBPS/PAN, 350×350 for UPSC).\n3. Set the target file size to 20 KB. VexaTool runs a binary search on the JPEG quality value to land at or just under the cap.\n4. Preview the result at 100% zoom. If facial features look soft, raise the target by 10–20 KB (most portals accept up to 40 KB even when the spec says 20 KB).\n5. Download the file and upload it to the portal. The file is saved as a clean .jpg with no metadata.\n"}, {"heading": "Best practices for keeping the photo acceptable to the portal", "body_md": "• Always shoot in landscape orientation against a plain white wall — auto-cropping is then trivial.\n• Avoid HDR and ''Portrait'' modes on iPhone — they add an extra HEIC layer that breaks signature recognition.\n• Do not screenshot the photo. Screenshots include UI chrome and break the aspect ratio.\n• Strip EXIF metadata before upload (VexaTool does this automatically on export).\n• If your portal accepts both JPG and PNG, choose JPG — PNG never compresses as small for photographic content.\n\nCommon size targets across Indian portals:\n\nTarget  | Where you will see it\n------- | -------------------------------\n20 KB   | SSC photo box, old PSC portals\n50 KB   | PAN, Aadhaar update, IBPS, SBI\n100 KB  | RRB, college admission portals\n200 KB  | NEET, JEE Main, NTA forms\n300 KB  | UPSC OTR\n"}, {"heading": "Privacy and why in-browser processing matters here", "body_md": "A photograph is biometric data — it identifies you. Uploading it to an online resizer means trusting that operator with your face for an unknown retention period. VexaTool removes that risk entirely: the image is processed in your browser using the HTML5 Canvas API, never sent to a server, never logged, never stored. Closing the tab erases everything."}, {"heading": "Acceptable formats, EXIF and colour profiles", "body_md": "Most Indian government portals accept JPEG only. PNG is rejected at IBPS, SBI, SSC and UPSC, even though the file is smaller, because their image validator expects baseline JPEG markers. VexaTool always writes a baseline JPEG with the sRGB colour profile and no EXIF metadata — this is the safest combination across every portal we have tested.\n\nIf your source is HEIC (iPhone) or AVIF (modern Android), the tool decodes it transparently. If your source is a PDF page, use the PDF-to-JPG converter first, then bring the JPG here. If your source is a screenshot, retake the photo — screenshots include device UI chrome and are almost always rejected by face-detection validators.\n\nFinally, a note on Adobe RGB and CMYK: studio cameras sometimes embed these wider colour profiles. They look identical on screen but trigger rejections on older portals. VexaTool strips them on export, so the output is universally accepted."}]'::jsonb, faqs = '[{"q": "Will my photo still be recognisable at 20 KB?", "a": "For a typical 200×230 passport-size photo, 20 KB is comfortable for the human eye and for portal validation. If the photo is much larger (e.g. 1200×1600) and you compress without resizing, faces may look soft — pick the resize preset instead."}, {"q": "Does the tool change the dimensions of my image?", "a": "Compress mode keeps the original dimensions and only reduces the file weight. Resize mode lets you set both target dimensions and target file size. Pick the mode that matches your portal requirement."}, {"q": "Why does the output overshoot the target by a few KB?", "a": "JPEG file size depends on image entropy — busy backgrounds compress less than plain ones. VexaTool runs a second pass automatically if the first overshoots 20 KB."}, {"q": "Is HEIC (iPhone format) supported?", "a": "Yes. The tool transparently decodes HEIC, HEIF, AVIF and WebP and re-encodes the output as a clean baseline JPEG that all government portals accept."}, {"q": "Can I batch-process several photos?", "a": "Yes — drag multiple files at once; each one is processed in sequence and downloaded as a ZIP."}, {"q": "Is there any watermark or sign-up?", "a": "No. VexaTool is free, has no daily limit and no account requirement. Output files are watermark-free."}]'::jsonb, internal_links = '[{"href": "/compress-image", "label": "Image Compressor (any KB)"}, {"href": "/image-resizer", "label": "Image Resizer (custom dimensions)"}, {"href": "/image-format-converter", "label": "Image Format Converter"}, {"href": "/background-remover", "label": "Background Remover"}, {"href": "/passport-photo-resize", "label": "Passport-Size Photo Maker"}, {"href": "/aadhaar-photo-resize", "label": "Aadhaar Photo Resizer"}, {"href": "/govt-job-photo-resize", "label": "Govt Job Photo Resizer"}, {"href": "/image-tools", "label": "All Image Tools"}]'::jsonb, breadcrumbs = '[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "Image Tools", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "Compress Image", "href": "/compress-image"}, {"name": "Resize to 20 KB", "href": "#"}]'::jsonb, parent_tool_slug = 'image-resizer', canonical_url = 'https://vexatool.com/resize-image-to-20kb', updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'resize-image-to-20kb';

