KB. VexaTool runs a binary search on the JPEG quality value to land at or just under the cap.\n4. Preview the result at 100% zoom. If facial features look soft, raise the target by 10–20 KB (most portals accept up to 100 KB even when the spec says 50 KB).\n5. Download the file and upload it to the portal. The file is saved as a clean .jpg with no metadata.\n"}, {"heading": "Best practices for keeping the photo acceptable to the portal", "body_md": "• Always shoot in landscape orientation against a plain white wall — auto-cropping is then trivial.\n• Avoid HDR and ''Portrait'' modes on iPhone — they add an extra HEIC layer that breaks signature recognition.\n• Do not screenshot the photo. Screenshots include UI chrome and break the aspect ratio.\n• Strip EXIF metadata before upload (VexaTool does this automatically on export).\n• If your portal accepts both JPG and PNG, choose JPG — PNG never compresses as small for photographic content.\n\nCommon size targets across Indian portals:\n\nTarget  | Where you will see it\n------- | -------------------------------\n20 KB   | SSC photo box, old PSC portals\n50 KB   | PAN, Aadhaar update, IBPS, SBI\n100 KB  | RRB, college admission portals\n200 KB  | NEET, JEE Main, NTA forms\n300 KB  | UPSC OTR\n"}, {"heading": "Privacy and why in-browser processing matters here", "body_md": "A photograph is biometric data — it identifies you. Uploading it to an online resizer means trusting that operator with your face for an unknown retention period. VexaTool removes that risk entirely: the image is processed in your browser using the HTML5 Canvas API, never sent to a server, never logged, never stored. Closing the tab erases everything."}, {"heading": "Acceptable formats, EXIF and colour profiles", "body_md": "Most Indian government portals accept JPEG only. PNG is rejected at IBPS, SBI, SSC and UPSC, even though the file is smaller, because their image validator expects baseline JPEG markers. VexaTool always writes a baseline JPEG with the sRGB colour profile and no EXIF metadata — this is the safest combination across every portal we have tested.\n\nIf your source is HEIC (iPhone) or AVIF (modern Android), the tool decodes it transparently. If your source is a PDF page, use the PDF-to-JPG converter first, then bring the JPG here. If your source is a screenshot, retake the photo — screenshots include device UI chrome and are almost always rejected by face-detection validators.\n\nFinally, a note on Adobe RGB and CMYK: studio cameras sometimes embed these wider colour profiles. They look identical on screen but trigger rejections on older portals. VexaTool strips them on export, so the output is universally accepted."}]'::jsonb, faqs = '[{"q": "Will my photo still be recognisable at 50 KB?", "a": "For a typical 200×230 passport-size photo, 50 KB is comfortable for the human eye and for portal validation. If the photo is much larger (e.g. 1200×1600) and you compress without resizing, faces may look soft — pick the resize preset instead."}, {"q": "Does the tool change the dimensions of my image?", "a": "Compress mode keeps the original dimensions and only reduces the file weight. Resize mode lets you set both target dimensions and target file size. Pick the mode that matches your portal requirement."}, {"q": "Why does the output overshoot the target by a few KB?", "a": "JPEG file size depends on image entropy — busy backgrounds compress less than plain ones. VexaTool runs a second pass automatically if the first overshoots 50 KB."}, {"q": "Is HEIC (iPhone format) supported?", "a": "Yes. The tool transparently decodes HEIC, HEIF, AVIF and WebP and re-encodes the output as a clean baseline JPEG that all government portals accept."}, {"q": "Can I batch-process several photos?", "a": "Yes — drag multiple files at once; each one is processed in sequence and downloaded as a ZIP."}, {"q": "Is there any watermark or sign-up?", "a": "No. VexaTool is free, has no daily limit and no account requirement. Output files are watermark-free."}]'::jsonb, internal_links = '[{"href": "/compress-image", "label": "Image Compressor (any KB)"}, {"href": "/image-resizer", "label": "Image Resizer (custom dimensions)"}, {"href": "/image-format-converter", "label": "Image Format Converter"}, {"href": "/background-remover", "label": "Background Remover"}, {"href": "/passport-photo-resize", "label": "Passport-Size Photo Maker"}, {"href": "/aadhaar-photo-resize", "label": "Aadhaar Photo Resizer"}, {"href": "/govt-job-photo-resize", "label": "Govt Job Photo Resizer"}, {"href": "/image-tools", "label": "All Image Tools"}]'::jsonb, breadcrumbs = '[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "Image Tools", "href": "/image-tools"}, {"name": "Compress Image", "href": "/compress-image"}, {"name": "Resize to 50 KB", "href": "#"}]'::jsonb, parent_tool_slug = 'image-resizer', canonical_url = 'https://vexatool.com/resize-image-to-50kb', updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'resize-image-to-50kb';

